<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Garage building in Chestermere is governed by the City of Chestermere, not the City of Calgary, even though the two sit side by side east of the Calgary boundary. The City's Land Use Bylaw No. 020-24 sets its own height, setback, size and lot coverage limits for accessory buildings. A garage plan drawn to Calgary numbers can land on a Chestermere lot and be wrong in several places.</p><p>This site is advertising. It puts Chestermere homeowners in touch with independent garage builders who quote and contract directly with you. It builds nothing, pulls no permits and holds no licence. Call now at (403) 555-0162 and ask for two or three comparable written quotes, and ask each builder which bylaw they are drawing to.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Chestermere</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Chestermere Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">New detached garages</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A single or double garage on a Chestermere lot. The bylaw defines a garage as a detached building over 10 m2 and up to 50 m2 for on-site parking, so the footprint you choose matters. See <a href="/detached-garages/">detached garages</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Garage packages</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Standard sizes with a set list of inclusions, which makes quotes easier to compare side by side. Check each size against Chestermere's 50 m2 garage limit before you sign anything. See <a href="/garage-packages/">garage packages</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Custom and oversized garages</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Tall doors, a triple bay or a workshop. In Chestermere, anything over 50 m2 is classed as an Accessory Building, Other, which is discretionary in the R-1 district. See <a href="/custom-garages/">custom garages</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E2DED6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#17191C;margin:0 0 8px;">Replacing an old garage</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Tearing down a tired garage and putting up a new one on the same lot. Ask the City what applies to the demolition, and have the builder spell out who removes the old slab. See <a href="/garage-replacement/">garage replacement</a>.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
